INT. COMMUNITY LAUNDROMAT-TURNED-CO-WORKING SPACE - DAY

Washers and dryers still line the walls, now labeled "Focus Pods." Beanbags sit on folding tables. A neon sign reads: SYNERGY SPIN.

At a long table, a quarterly planning meeting is underway.

GREGORY "GREG" ABERNATHY-LIU, 40s, founder, pacing in a gilet. He holds a clicker connected to nothing.

TAMSIN HOLLOWAY, 30s, head of People, takes minutes on a laptop with a sticker reading "Be Kind."

OSWALDO PINTO, 50s, finance, eats an apple methodically and watches the spreadsheet on the wall.

FATIMA AL-RASHID, 20s, junior designer, sits very still on a beanbag, holding a mug in both hands.

KENNETH "KEN" BOATENG, 30s, engineer, has headphones around his neck and a drying rack sock stuck to his sleeve.

At the end of the table, ROSALIND MCCREADY, 60s, investor, in a trench coat, listens without taking it off.

GREG
So, Q3. Big wins. Big, big wins.

OSWALDO
We lost forty thousand dollars.

GREG
In a growth mindset, that's investment.

OSWALDO
In a finance mindset, that's forty thousand dollars.

TAMSIN
Let's hold space for both framings.

KEN
Can we hold space for the dryer? It's been beeping for ten minutes.

FATIMA
It's mine. It has my lunch in it.

KEN
Why is your lunch in a dryer?

FATIMA
It's the only thing that gets warm.

Rosalind sets down her pen.

ROSALIND
Greg, what is the burn rate?

GREG
Healthy.

OSWALDO
Fourteen thousand a month.

ROSALIND
And revenue?

GREG
We're pre-revenue.

OSWALDO
We're pre-everything.

TAMSIN
Oswaldo, let's try to stay solutions-oriented.

OSWALDO
The solution is a loan officer.

Greg clicks the clicker. Nothing happens. He clicks harder.

GREG
This is our roadmap.

The wall flashes. A slide: a drawing of a washing machine with a rocket strapped to it.

FATIMA
(quietly)
I drew that at two a.m.

ROSALIND
It is... bold.

GREG
Thank you, Rosalind.

ROSALIND
That was not praise.

KEN
Does the rocket actually work?

GREG
It's a metaphor.

KEN
For what?

GREG
For ascent.

OSWALDO
Of the debt.

Tamsin types it down. Deletes it. Types it again.

TAMSIN
I'm recording "alignment challenges."

ROSALIND
Record that I'm leaving in five minutes.

GREG
We haven't done the offsite.

ROSALIND
Where is the offsite?

GREG
Also here. Tomorrow. With cake.

FATIMA
Is the cake in the dryer?

Ken laughs. Stops. Looks at Greg, who is not laughing.

KEN
Sorry.

GREG
We don't apologise for joy at Synergy Spin.

OSWALDO
(low)
We apologise for invoices.

The dryer buzzes for the last time. Fatima rises, opens its round door, and pulls out a steaming paper bag. She sets it on the table and unfolds it carefully.

A sandwich. Slightly flattened. Warm.

She offers half to Rosalind.

Rosalind studies it. Takes it.

ROSALIND
This is the best thing I have seen all quarter.

GREG
(stricken)
We have a roadmap.

ROSALIND
You have a sandwich.

She bites into it. Greg turns back to the wall, clicker raised, and the rocket flashes on, and on.

TAMSIN
Moving to Q4.
